      "side": 1,
      "message": "Skia is currently going through a \"should Skia convert from using SkSpan to std::span\" decision (Skia very recently started requiring C++20), so I think Skia would prefer not to add an SkSpan API right now if it can be avoided. I think the current state of things is to prefer `std::span` for new API.\n\nAlso, to better indicate intent this should be a span of `std::byte`.\n\nSo I think this should be `std::span\u003cconst std::byte\u003e`.",
      "revId": "bb364cf9a2305286bc6145c3852684230837ef6a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
